arget_length)` until the TODO in there for providing offsets/length is done\r\n\r\nThat works for my case, but there are actual tests for this https://github.com/openxla/iree/blob/13de9f3bf706938027fcac9cccc89a02ff7d2ac6/runtime/bindings/python/tests/hal_test.py#L294\r\nIs there some way to get the expected alignment for a buffer like this?","created_at":"2023-11-09T17:00:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/15508#issuecomment-1804209501","id":1804209501,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/15508","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M5rig1d","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1804209501/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-11-09T17:00:17Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1804209501","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22101546?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qedawkins","id":22101546,"login":"qedawkins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTAxNTQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Actually I see the byte offset and length is already on the `iree_hal_buffer_t` https://github.com/openxla/iree/blob/13de9f3bf706938027fcac9cccc89a02ff7d2ac6/runtime/src/iree/hal/buffer.h#L856\r\n\r\nAnd the HalBuffer class looks a reference to an `iree_hal_buffer_t` https://github.com/openxla/iree/blob/13de9f3bf706938027fcac9cccc89a02ff7d2ac6/runtime/bindings/python/hal.h#L175\r\n\r\nHow hard would it be to just use the offsets/lengths directly?","created_at":"2023-11-09T17:04:30Z","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/15508#issuecomment-1804216823","id":1804216823,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/15508","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M5riin3","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1804216823/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-11-09T17:04:39Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1804216823","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22101546?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qedawkins","id":22101546,"login":"qedawkins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTAxNTQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"I can look when at my desk. I don't think alignment will be a problem. An allocation sufficient for a 4byte transaction will always be sufficient for a two byte one.","created_at":"2023-11-09T17:09:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/15508#issuecomment-1804225127","id":1804225127,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/15508","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M5rikpn","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1804225127/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-11-09T17:09:19Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1804225127","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/494208?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stellaraccident","id":494208,"login":"stellaraccident","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NDIwOA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"> I can look when at my desk. I don't think alignment will be a problem. An allocation sufficient for a 4byte transaction will always be sufficient for a two byte one.\r\n\r\nMakes sense, just trying to understand the reasoning behind the original check. If `source < target` is always fine then that works for me.","created_at":"2023-11-09T17:11:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/15508#issuecomment-1804229666","id":1804229666,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/15508","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M5rilwi","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1804229666/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-11-09T17:11:09Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1804229666","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22101546?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qedawkins","id":22101546,"login":"qedawkins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTAxNTQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"# Problem description\r\nThe following python code will fail with the following error\r\n```\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/home/quinn/model_testing/only_conv.py\", line 116, in <module>\r\n    print(iree_output.to_host())\r\n          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"/home/quinn/iree-build/runtime/bindings/python/iree/runtime/array_interop.py\", line 107, in to_host\r\n    self._transfer_to_host(False)\r\n  File \"/home/quinn/iree-build/runtime/bindings/python/iree/runtime/array_interop.py\", line 135, in _transfer_to_host\r\n    self._host_array = self._copy_to_host()\r\n                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"/home/quinn/iree-build/runtime/bindings/python/iree/runtime/array_interop.py\", line 162, in _copy_to_host\r\n    self._device.queue_copy(\r\nValueError: Source and target buffer length must match and it does not. Please check allocations\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport torch\r\n\r\nmodule = \"\"\"\r\n#map = affine_map<(d0, d1) -> (d0, d1)>\r\n#map1 = affine_map<(d0, d1) -> (d0)>\r\nmodule {\r\n  func.func @forward(%arg0: tensor<1x?xf16>) -> tensor<1xf16> {\r\n    %c1 = arith.constant 1 : index\r\n    %dim = tensor.dim %arg0, %c1 : tensor<1x?xf16>\r\n    %0 = tensor.empty(%dim) : tensor<1x?xf16>\r\n    %c1_0 = arith.constant 1 : index\r\n    %dim_1 = tensor.dim %arg0, %c1_0 : tensor<1x?xf16>\r\n    %1 = tensor.empty() : tensor<1xf16>\r\n    %cst = arith.constant -6.550400e+04 : f16\r\n    %res = flow.dispatch.region -> (tensor<1xf16>) {\r\n      %2 = linalg.fill ins(%cst : f16) outs(%1 : tensor<1xf16>) -> tensor<1xf16>\r\n      %3 = linalg.generic {indexing_maps = [#map, #map1], iterator_types = [\"parallel\", \"reduction\"]} ins(%arg0 : tensor<1x?xf16>) outs(%2 : tensor<1xf16>) {\r\n      ^bb0(%in: f16, %out: f16):\r\n        %7 = arith.maximumf %in, %out : f16\r\n        linalg.yield %7 : f16\r\n      } -> tensor<1xf16>\r\n      %cst_2 = arith.constant 0.000000e+00 : f16\r\n      %4 = linalg.fill ins(%cst_2 : f16) outs(%1 : tensor<1xf16>) -> tensor<1xf16>\r\n      %5 = linalg.generic {indexing_maps = [#map, #map1, #map1], iterator_types = [\"parallel\", \"reduction\"]} ins(%arg0, %3 : tensor<1x?xf16>, tensor<1xf16>) outs(%4 : tensor<1xf16>) {\r\n      ^bb0(%in: f16, %in_3: f16, %out: f16):\r\n        %7 = arith.subf %in, %in_3 : f16\r\n        %8 = math.exp %7 : f16\r\n        %9 = arith.addf %8, %out : f16\r\n        linalg.yield %9 : f16\r\n      } -> tensor<1xf16>\r\n      flow.return %5 : tensor<1xf16>\r\n    }\r\n    return %res : tensor<1xf16>\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\nexample_input = torch.FloatTensor([[2.0, 0.0]]).half()\r\n\r\n# Run through IREE vulkan\r\nimport iree.runtime as ireert\r\nfrom iree.runtime import get_driver, get_device\r\nimport iree.compiler as ireec\r\n\r\ndevice = \"vulkan\"\r\nruntime_device = \"vulkan\"\r\n\r\nflatbuffer = ireec.compile_str(\r\n    module,\r\n    target_backends=[device],\r\n    extra_args=[\r\n        \"--iree-vulkan-target-triple=rdna3-unknown-linux\",\r\n        \"--iree-stream-resource-index-bits=64\",\r\n        \"--iree-vm-target-index-bits=64\",\r\n        ],\r\n)\r\n\r\nconfig = ireert.Config(driver_name=runtime_device)\r\nvm_module = ireert.VmModule.from_flatbuffer(config.vm_instance, flatbuffer)\r\nctx = ireert.SystemContext(config=config)\r\nctx.add_vm_module(vm_module)\r\nforward = ctx.modules.module[\"forward\"]\r\niree_output = forward(example_input.numpy())\r\n\r\n# Fails due to a size mismatch between the source and target buffer\r\nprint(iree_output.to_host())\r\n```\r\n\r\n# Investigation\r\n\r\nThe source (device) buffer will be `2` bytes for the single f16, however when trying to allocate the host buffer to copy into (https://github.com/openxla/iree/blob/d991dc9330d486b804a204e6e18f8287c256def1/runtime/bindings/python/iree/runtime/array_interop.py#L153), it ends up padding the allocation to `4` bytes, causing the sizes to mismatch.\r\n","closed_at":"2023-11-09T21:36:18Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22101546?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/qedawkins","id":22101546,"login":"qedawkins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTAxNTQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qedawkins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments":5,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/15508/comments","created_at":"2023-11-09T14:53:46Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/15508/events","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/15508","id":1985796175,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":false,"description":"Something isn't working","id":1553038945,"name":"bug 🐞","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNTUzMDM4OTQ1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/labels/bug%20%F0%9F%90%9E"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"fbc4fc","default":false,"description":"Relating to the IREE runtime library","id":1921021839,"name":"runtime","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxOTIxMDIxODM5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/labels/runtime"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"22ad75","default":false,"description":"Python wrapping IREE's C API","id":2524353575,"name":"bindings/python","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNTI0MzUzNTc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/labels/bindings/python"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.co